 and Daechi 2-dong stretches.\nRelations. Shares spare-part conditions with neighboring sections'' maintenance staff. When quarreling with neighboring stations over fuel and food allocation, he takes the public ledger as the standard.\n\n- Affiliation: Arc\n- Occupation: Duty Roster · Custody of Original Will\n- Rank: Stationmaster\n- Title: Stationmaster\n- O Gyeongjae''s work in the Arc district is connected to Samseong 1-dong.\n- O Gyeongjae''s work in duty service and custody of the original wills is connected to Jongno 5·6-ga-dong."},"biography":"**Life.** Generation of 2126. O Gyeongjae was the last duty apprentice in the Samseong underground passage. As a member of the O clan, he took over the shutter-check sheets and the fuel and food ledgers and became Samseong''s stationmaster. He walked the Sinsa-dong, Nonhyeon 1-dong and Daechi 2-dong stretches gathering patrol records, and did not accept the demand to increase night lighting. It was agreed that the original box of machine-body repair records would be sealed jointly with the neighboring section''s staff.\nOffice. Rank: Stationmaster. Title: Stationmaster.\nFamily. O Gyeongjae comes from the O clan. He is responsible for the Samseong, Sinsa-dong, Nonhyeon 1-dong and Daechi 2-dong stretches.\nRelations. Shares spare-part conditions with neighboring sections'' maintenance staff. When quarreling with neighboring stations over fuel and food allocation, he takes the public ledger as the standard.\n\n- Affiliation: Arc\n- Occupation: Duty Roster · Custody of Original Will\n- Rank: Stationmaster\n- Title: Stationmaster\n- O Gyeongjae''s work in the Arc district is connected to Samseong 1-dong.\n- O Gyeongjae''s work in duty service and custody of the original wills is connected to Jongno 5·6-ga-dong.","relations":{"outgoing":[{"from":"O Gyeongjae","type":"Contract","to":"Im Hajun","basis":"After Im Hajun''s disappearance, checks the pump-maintenance records he left, as Stationmaster of Samseong Station"},{"from"