clan":{"id":"adfc-ccad-c8fc","name":"Geun Clan of Cheongju","crest":"clan-crests/adfc-ccad-c8fc.svg"},"generation":"opening","minors":false,"sourceKind":"proposal","values":{"Authority":-25,"Openness":30,"Force":-20,"Material":5,"Communal":10,"Principle":20,"Public":35,"Eligibility":20,"Dispersed":35,"Transformative":15},"desire":{"Longing":-10,"Monopoly":25,"Risk":5,"Display":10,"Sustained":15,"Orientation":"Fluid","Union":"Polyamorous"},"fields":{"Livelihood":"Recording signatures and voting attendance","Affiliation":"Arc","Community Role":"Guild Member","Duty":"Arc Signing Clerk","Values":"Authority −25 | Openness 30 | Force −20 | Materiality 5 | Community 10 | Principle 20 | Disclosure 35 | Qualification 20 | Decentralization 35 | Transformation 15","Desires":"Craving −10 | Monopoly 25 | Risk 5 | Display 10 | Persistence 15 | Orientation Fluid | Bonding Multi-partner"},"sections":{"Life":"Geun Juha, born on 2099-07-01, keeps the machine-body parts in-and-out ledger at the Arc workshop in winter. On every day parts change hands, Geun checks the quantity and the person handing over, and distinguishes offices conferred by the government from roles within the Arc.\n- Geun Juha keeps the machine-body parts in-and-out ledger at the Arc workshop. This work does not determine residence, exact facility boundaries, rank, holding, or tenure rights.","Duty":"The community role is guild member, and the duty is recording the machine-body parts in-and-out ledger. This duty is an internal function of the Arc and is neither a Government of the Republic of Korea civil-service office nor a rank.","Anecdote":"","Relationships":"","Goals":"Geun Juha seeks to keep the workshop ledger in order so that the quantities and handover records of the machine-body parts ledger can always be verified.","Fear":"That the quantities or handover records in the parts ledger are altered, so that Geun Juha''s scope of responsibility and the repair order collapse together.","Intervention":"Geun Juha can cross-check the relevant signatures and handover times and can make the records public, but cannot confer new offices, ranks, rights, or holdings."},"biography":"In winter, Geun Juha first cross-checks the machine-body parts in-and-out records against the stock sheet at the Arc workshop. On days when outside machines come near or parts run short, Geun records the receipt time and handover order in the same ledger.\n\n- Livelihood: Recording signatures and voting attendance\n- Affiliation: Arc\n- Community Role: Guild Member\n- Duty: Arc Signing Clerk\n**Life.** Geun Juha, born on 2099-07-01, keeps the machine-body parts in-and-out ledger at the Arc workshop in winter. On every day parts change hands, Geun checks the quantity and the person handing over, and distinguishes offices conferred by the government from roles within the Arc.\n- Geun Juha keeps the machine-body parts in-and-out ledger at the Arc workshop. This work does not determine residence, exact facility boundaries, rank, holding, or tenure rights.\n\n**Duty.** The community role is guild member, and the duty is recording the machine-body parts in-and-out ledger. This duty is an internal function of the Arc and is neither a Government of the Republic of Korea civil-service office nor a rank.\n\n**Goal.** Geun Juha seeks to keep the workshop ledger in order so that the quantities and handover records of the machine-body parts ledger can always be verified.\n\n**Fear.** That the quantities or handover records in the parts ledger are altered, so that Geun Juha''s scope of responsibility and the repair order collapse together.\n\n**Intervention.** Geun Juha can cross-check the relevant signatures and handover times and can make the records public, but cannot confer new offices, ranks, rights, or holdings.\n\n::: details Appendix — Ledger Numbers\n\n- Values: Authority −25 | Openness 30 | Force −20 | Materiality 5 | Community 10 | Principle 20 | Disclosure 35 | Qualification 20 | Decentralization 35 | Tran